</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/588f3c36-df0f-11f1-b3bf-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/6816aa54a64f20da410fe06c62ff522af2f50eb2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/588f3c36-df0f-11f1-b3bf-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/6816aa54a64f20da410fe06c62ff522af2f50eb2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7648d1a4-de30-11f1-96c5-0f09eed6c61f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:31:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/588f3c36-df0f-11f1-b3bf-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/6816aa54a64f20da410fe06c62ff522af2f50eb2.jpg">© John Macdougall, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Democrat Scott Colom wins historic Senate race in Mississippi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-democrat-scott-colom-wins-historic-senate-race-in-mississippi</link><description>
Democrat Scott Colom defeated Republican Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith in Mississippi after a final count on Wednesday, becoming the state's first Black US senator since Reconstruction. His narrow victory adds to the Democrats' midterm gains as President Donald Trump's party suffers a series of defeats.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7807fc4-de27-11f1-b242-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314768923953.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7807fc4-de27-11f1-b242-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314768923953.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3af0db02-de2a-11f1-b2bd-4955f5751d59</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:47:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7807fc4-de27-11f1-b242-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314768923953.jpg">© Ellen Schmidt, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo XIV returns to second homeland Peru and a nationwide welcome</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-xiv-returns-to-second-homeland-peru-to-a-nationwide-welcome</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV arrived in Peru on Wednesday for the final leg of his South American tour, returning to the country where he spent more than two decades as a missionary and bishop. Thousands gathered to welcome him home as “Padre Robert”, with many hoping his visit will bring attention to the country's poverty, crime and political instability.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c7939ee-de21-11f1-adfe-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T224025Z-451595732-RC2YLOAKZZON-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c7939ee-de21-11f1-adfe-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T224025Z-451595732-RC2YLOAKZZON-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">afeb08d4-de29-11f1-81c1-8fedcbdbcc33</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:43:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c7939ee-de21-11f1-adfe-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T224025Z-451595732-RC2YLOAKZZON-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Failed state: Haiti has collapsed in a kind of a black hole'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bukele-says-salvadoran-troops-destroyed-gang-hq-in-haiti</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Jean Marie Théodat, Author and Head of the Geography Department at Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne University. He describes Haiti as a failed state: "Haiti has collapsed in a kind of a black hole. I mean there is no president, no elections, no chambers of deputies, no senators." Addressing the reported deployment of Salvadoran troops to Haiti, he says “when you are dying, you don't look at the hand that brings help,” explaining why many Haitians may welcome military assistance from Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele despite concerns about his government's authoritarian methods and the uncertain political consequences of foreign intervention. Drawing on a Haitian proverb, he warns that “a goat with several masters can die of thirst while tied up,” underscoring the dangers of poorly coordinated interventions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f6655d8-dded-11f1-926e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-151842-152903-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f6655d8-dded-11f1-926e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-151842-152903-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33f1f422-dded-11f1-8600-530574a1d80e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:38:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil electoral court fines Meta $1.3 MN, sees no deliberate election bias</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-1-3-mn-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias</link><description>
